{"name":"Liminality","hex":"#dad79b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"liminality","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fact of being on the border of, or in between, two states.","The state or quality of ambiguity which exists in the middle stage of certain events or rituals (such as a rite of passage or a society-wide revolution), during which the participating individual or group no longer holds its pre-ritual status but has not yet attained the status it will hold when the ritual has been completed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liminality"}],"entries":[{"title":"Liminality","blocks":[{"text":"In anthropology, liminality is the quality of ambiguity or disorientation that occurs in the middle stage of a rite of passage, when participants no longer hold their pre-ritual status but have not yet begun the transition to the status they will hold when the rite is complete. During a rite's liminal stage, participants \"stand at the threshold\" between their previous way of structuring their identity, time, or community, and a new way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Initiation_ritual_of_boys_in_Malawi.jpg/330px-Initiation_ritual_of_boys_in_Malawi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liminality","wikidata":"Q1825499"},{"title":"Liminality (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Liminality is the seventh studio album by Irish ambient musician Seamus Ó Muíneacháin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Liminality_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liminality_(album)","wikidata":"Q130271363"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Cole_Thomas_The_Course_of_Empire_Destruction_1836.jpg/500px-Cole_Thomas_The_Course_of_Empire_Destruction_1836.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o